# Independent Transfiguration update channel; match the launcher's external
# TRANSFIGURATION_UPDATE_REPOSITORY and TRANSFIGURATION_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY config.
TRANSFIGURATION_UPDATE_REPOSITORY=owner/Transfiguration
TRANSFIGURATION_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY=

# Supply exactly one Ed25519 private-key source only during explicit --mode sign.
# No key value is bundled in this file, the component ZIP, or review output.
# Keep the key file outside the source, production payload and output directories.
TRANSFIGURATION_UPDATE_SIGNING_KEY_PEM=
TRANSFIGURATION_UPDATE_SIGNING_KEY_FILE=

# The publisher defaults to --mode review and emits an unsigned manifest.json.
# --mode sign additionally requires a clean pinned source checkout and external
# --verification-file plus --verification-sha256, then emits signed updates.json.
# Required CLI pins: --transfiguration-commit, --bridge-sha256,
# --source-compatibility-sha256. Source text payloads must match exact Git blobs
# (use an LF checkout for production artifacts; line endings are hashed).
# --launcher-requirement accepts stable full comparators joined by commas,
# for example >=0.1.0, <0.2.0. Component versions use stable X.Y.Z only.
#
# External proof JSON exact schema (real proof generator supplies actual hashes):
# protocol: 1
# kind: transfiguration_production_metadata
# transfiguration_commit: full lowercase 40-character reviewed source commit
# bridge_sha256: lowercase SHA-256 of the verified production DLL
# source_compatibility_sha256: lowercase SHA-256 of source compatibility.json
# native_client_version: source osu.Game.dll/osu!.dll version without final .0
# runtime / ruleset_api / harmony: exact source compatibility strings
# native_assemblies: exact five source assembly names mapped to lowercase SHA-256
# checks.production_browser_only: passed_compiled_policy
# checks.explicit_logout: passed_pinned_ui_metadata
# native_gui_and_login: pending_human_test
#
# The independent ZIP alone adds native_client_version to compatibility.json;
# manifest.files hashes the resulting payload, while the proof pins the original
# source compatibility bytes. The source compatibility schema remains unchanged.
#
# GitHub release workflow expects an existing immutable artifact containing:
# production/ (the exact ten build outputs, README.md is renamed inside the ZIP)
# production-verification.json (external proof, excluded from the component ZIP)
# Configure repository variables above and protect transfiguration-release with
# required reviewers before supplying its signing-key secret. Review is default;
# signing and optional draft release creation require explicit workflow inputs.
